cff-version: 1.2.0
message: Please cite the FringeScope version used, together with the relevant primary spectroscopy references.
type: software
title: 'FringeScope: Time-resolved step-scan FTIR artifact simulator'
abstract: FringeScope is an interactive forward simulator of artifacts in time-resolved step-scan FTIR
  spectroscopy. A declared synthetic photosystem I (PSI)-inspired difference signal with two bin-averaged exponential
  components and a causal non-decaying residual is compared with mirror-motion, optical-folding, continuous
  globar-leakage and pulsed 532 nm actinic-pickup models. Optional electrical pickup and registration
  mismatch are sensitivity models. Linked contour, spectrum, kinetic and decay-associated spectrum views
  are available in a Python/Qt desktop application and a browser edition using the same scientific engine.
  The source includes analytic model inputs, synthetic CSV examples, original simulated figures, equations
  and primary references. No experimental spectral matrix is distributed. Model agreement does not identify
  an experimental artifact mechanism.
authors:
- family-names: Nelson
  given-names: Michael Raymond
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9809-9842
version: 0.11.0
